{"nodes": [{"id": "chicken_behavior_analysis_main_chicken_behavior_analysis_main_img_frame02501", "label": "Frame 02501: Infrared Night View of Young Broilers with Sparse Feeder Attendance", "file_type": "image", "source_file": "Chicken-Behavior-Analysis-main/Chicken-Behavior-Analysis-main/img/frame02501.png", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": "2022-02-22T08:16:19", "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Monochrome infrared/low-light CCTV still, '1080P-IPC-Siren', 2022-02-22 08:16:19. Smaller, younger birds are loosely scattered in patchy clumps across a broad litter floor; the five pan feeders on the crossing feed line appear largely empty of feed, with only partial rings of birds attending them. The house perimeter wall and a floor-level cable/curtain line are visible at the bottom of the frame, and the wide-angle lens produces noticeable barrel distortion."}, {"id": "chicken_behavior_analysis_main_chicken_behavior_analysis_main_img_frame02501_infrared_night_capture", "label": "Infrared Night-Vision Capture Mode", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "Chicken-Behavior-Analysis-main/Chicken-Behavior-Analysis-main/img/frame02501.png", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Under dark-period lighting the camera switches to monochrome IR: colour cues vanish, the red feeder caps become indistinguishable from the pan body, contrast between bird and litter drops, and sensor noise rises. Roughly half of this chunk's frames are captured this way, so any model trained on the dataset must handle both appearance regimes."}, {"id": "chicken_behavior_analysis_main_chicken_behavior_analysis_main_img_frame02501_illumination_domain_shift", "label": "Colour/Infrared Illumination Domain Shift", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "Chicken-Behavior-Analysis-main/Chicken-Behavior-Analysis-main/img/frame02501.png", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Deliberately sampling both colour daylight frames and monochrome IR frames of the same scene forces a detector to rely on shape and texture rather than the strong white-bird-on-dark-litter colour contrast. The cost is a harder learning problem; the benefit is round-the-clock inference without a separate night model, which matters because feeding and resting behaviour differ most between light and dark periods."}], "edges": [{"source": "chicken_behavior_analysis_main_chicken_behavior_analysis_main_img_frame02501", "target": "chicken_behavior_analysis_main_chicken_behavior_analysis_main_img_frame02101_overhead_cctv_frame", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "Chicken-Behavior-Analysis-main/Chicken-Behavior-Analysis-main/img/frame02501.png", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "chicken_behavior_analysis_main_chicken_behavior_analysis_main_img_frame02501", "target": "chicken_behavior_analysis_main_chicken_behavior_analysis_main_img_frame02101_pan_feeder_line", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "Chicken-Behavior-Analysis-main/Chicken-Behavior-Analysis-main/img/frame02501.png", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "chicken_behavior_analysis_main_chicken_behavior_analysis_main_img_frame02501", "target": "chicken_behavior_analysis_main_chicken_behavior_analysis_main_img_frame025501_flock_dispersal_pattern", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "Chicken-Behavior-Analysis-main/Chicken-Behavior-Analysis-main/img/frame02501.png", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "chicken_behavior_analysis_main_chicken_behavior_analysis_main_img_frame02501", "target": "chicken_behavior_analysis_main_chicken_behavior_analysis_main_img_frame02501_infrared_night_capture", "relation": "implements", "confidence": "EX